{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'cat assignments/T-PAP-placement-aware-precision.md'","aggregated_output":"# Assignment T-PAP (campaign c2-resume, x86-main; owner Claude Opus; worker Codex) — factory technique: placement-aware expert precision (+ imatrix)\nHypothesis (orchestrator): with `--n-cpu-moe K` (experts of the FIRST K layers on CPU), the CPU part is DRAM-bandwidth bound (~26 GB/s on this Ryzen 7 3700X: 8 Q4_K experts x 0.84 MiB per layer per token in ~0.26 ms; D014/D022). Requantizing ONLY the CPU-resident layers' experts to fewer bits (Q3_K, Q2_K) should speed the CPU part ~proportionally to bytes and cut host RAM, while GPU layers keep Q4_K; quality loss is confined to K layers. D013: all-layer 3-bit experts KLD 0.135 (vs 0.040 at 4-bit), 2-bit collapses (0.77) — WITHOUT imatrix; imatrix calibration untried and likely helps low bits.\nTools: the upstream image ghcr.io/ggml-org/llama.cpp@sha256:395d01bb... has llama-quantize/llama-imatrix but you cannot run Docker. So build CPU-only llama-quantize + llama-imatrix from a scratch tree (artifacts/codexPAP/tree = git archive ref/llama.cpp 31288c9c6; -DGGML_CUDA=OFF; -j4; nice). Source model: ~/models/campaign/gguf/granite-3.1-1b-a400m-instruct-bf16.gguf (read-only). mixE4K recipe (decisions/D013): `llama-quantize --tensor-type 'ffn_.*_exps=q4_K' bf16 out Q8_0`.\nDo: (1) imatrix: compute with llama-imatrix on CPU (-t 6) over wikitext-2 TRAIN text (~/models/campaign/data/wikitext/wikitext-2-raw/wiki.train.raw; bounded: e.g. --chunks 100 -c 512) -> artifacts/codexPAP/models/granite-wtrain.imatrix (record chunks, sha). Evaluation will use wiki.test -> disjoint. (2) Produce GGUFs into artifacts/codexPAP/models/ (llama-quantize supports per-tensor regex --tensor-type; verify exact syntax in-tree): for K in {12, 18, 24}: pap{K}_q3 (blk 0..K-1 experts q3_K, other experts q4_K, rest Q8_0), pap{K}_q2 (q2_K), each WITH imatrix, plus pap24_q3_noimat (= mixE3K-equivalent control w/o imatrix) and mix4_imat (all experts q4_K with imatrix) control. Record file sizes, per-layer types (verify by reading tensors with gguf-py), sha256. (3) Write lab tests JSON lab-tests-pap.json (schema: lab/tests/match1.json + mem2.json kl_q8 for KLD: `llama-perplexity -c 512 --chunks 20 -ngl 99 --kl-divergence-base /out/bf16.kl --kl-divergence` with docker_args mount of artifacts/kl) covering: decode at matching --n-cpu-moe K for each pap{K} AND the mixE4K baseline at same K; KLD for every model; files must be referenced by basename (orchestrator will place them in one model dir). (4) Optional cheap CPU sanity: KLD on CPU for pap12_q3 only if bf16.kl compatible (else skip).\nDeliver cc/pap/{make_pap.sh (reproducible recipe), README.md (technique, integration conditions: llama.cpp --n-cpu-moe offloads first K layers — verify in source and cite line; types per layer; imatrix provenance; claims allowed)}, artifacts/codexPAP/{models/*, MANIFEST.json, lab-tests-pap.json}. Allowed writes: cc/pap/**, artifacts/codexPAP/**. 75 min, no Docker, no network, -j4, nice. Checkpoint at 50 min. Final message: files + sizes, imatrix provenance, exact tests, gaps.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
